Post-installation setup for the Db2 service
Last Updated: 2026-03-26

After you install the Db2 service on IBM® Software Hub, you must configure settings specifically for your environment before provisioning an instance.

    Creating a service instance for Db2
    After you install Db2, you must create at least one Db2 service instance in the operands project. You can choose the method or methods that you want to use to create service instances.
    Deploying Db2 with limited privileges
    You can improve security by running the Db2 container on IBM Software Hub with limited privileges.
    Upgrading the license before you deploy Db2
    After you install the Db2 service, you can upgrade your license from Db2 Community Edition to Db2 Advanced Edition.
    Configuring tethered namespaces for the Db2 service
    You can configure tethered namespaces for your Db2 databases to isolate specific databases or workloads.
    Advanced configuration for demanding workloads in Db2
    You can manually update the CRI-O configuration of the Red Hat® OpenShift® system where Db2 is running with or without Machine Config to handle advanced configurations and demanding workloads.
    Disabling database connection validation for Db2 after installation or upgrade
    You can disable the validation check for all Db2 database connections.

